cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software

title: "Algebraic Definitional Leakage in Paired Biomedical Prediction Models and a Reproducible Audit Framework"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-31"

abstract: >
  A fully reproducible benchmark for algebraic definitional leakage in paired
  biomedical prediction models. Provides a synthetic paired-outcome generator,
  an 8-type leakage taxonomy with quantified AUROC inflation, a cross-classifier
  SHAP attribution distortion analysis, and the Paired Outcome Leakage Reporting
  Checklist (POLRC) validated against 15 published paired-biomarker studies
  across four real-world clinical cohorts (CGMacros, ICU Glucose, eICU, MIMIC-IV).

